big-fella: amdgpu CRC capture leaves a Dolby Vision tunnel stream's formatter alone

A CRTC CRC capture (debugfs crtc-N/crc, source "crtc") switches the stream to
TRUN8 truncation without dynamic expansion, so it would measure another FMT
setup than the tunnel's (dither and truncation off). Leave a tunnel stream as
it is, so the CRC measures exactly what goes to the TV. From CB1's
linux-9921-amd-dv-diagnostic-and-vrr-guards.patch (CroqueMr/libreelec-x86-DV,
MIT). Applies after linux-9920-big-fella-amdgpu-dv-tunnel.patch.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_crc.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_crc.c
index db546dd..a8948ab 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_crc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_crc.c
@@ -616,8 +616,13 @@ int amdgpu_dm_crtc_configure_crc_source(struct drm_crtc *crtc,
 		}
 	}
 
-	/* Configure dithering */
-	if (!dm_need_crc_dither(source)) {
+	/* Configure dithering. big-fella: but never for a Dolby Vision tunnel
+	 * stream: its formatter setup (no dither, no truncation) is part of the
+	 * tunnel, and the CRC must measure that one (from CB1's linux-9921).
+	 */
+	if (stream_state->dv_lab) {
+		/* keep the tunnel's dither option and dynamic expansion */
+	} else if (!dm_need_crc_dither(source)) {
 		dc_stream_set_dither_option(stream_state, DITHER_OPTION_TRUN8);
 		dc_stream_set_dyn_expansion(stream_state->ctx->dc, stream_state,
 					    DYN_EXPANSION_DISABLE);
